  {
    rule: "Practise only on your own lab or on platforms built for it",
    why: "TryHackMe, PortSwigger's Web Security Academy and Hack The Box labs are made for practice. A school portal, a shop site or a friend's account is not, even if you mean no harm.",
  },
  {
    rule: "Report what you find through the owner's channel, and keep the data you touched to the minimum",
    why: "Bug bounty programs publish their rules and safe boundaries. Pulling out more data than you need to prove a bug can turn a good report into a legal problem.",
  },
  {
    rule: "Know that a disclosure policy is not a shield",
    why: "CERT-In's Responsible Vulnerability Disclosure and Coordination Policy (September 2021, as reported by MediaNama) aims to resolve a reported issue within 120 days of first contacting the vendor. It also says that reporting a vulnerability does not exempt you from compliance with the law. Digital rights groups have asked for a clearer safe harbour for researchers. So the permission still has to exist before you test.",
  },
];

