  <h2 id="ai">AI-assisted pentesting: what it squeezes and what it rewards</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools are now part of the offensive toolkit. XBOW, an AI pentesting company, said in 2025 that its autonomous
    tester reached the top of HackerOne's US leaderboard. By its own numbers about 1,060 reports were submitted, 130 had
    been resolved, and its team reviewed findings before submission. Those are the vendor's own figures, not independently
    checked. HackerOne's researcher survey found 70% of 1,820 respondents already use AI tools.
  </p>

